@@ -570,6 +570,17 @@ and pauses only accounts freshly confirmed at 100%; unknown or failed refreshes
 | `round-robin` | Evenly assign unbound requests across eligible accounts. `autoSwitchThreshold` does not change normal round-robin selection. `accountPoolStickyLimit` (1–100) counts assignments on one pick, not successful upstream responses. |
 | `fill-first` | Assign unbound requests to the active account until cooldown, reauthentication, or the configured drain threshold; unknown usage does not force a switch. Healthy bound tasks keep affinity. |
 
+With proactive switching enabled, `fill-first` and `round-robin` also move an existing bound task
+when its account reaches a reported 100% limit and another eligible account has genuine quota
+headroom and lower usage. This includes moving from an exhausted 5-hour account to a weekly-only
+main account; an absent 5-hour window does not exclude main. Below 100%, these strategies retain
+the binding. `autoSwitchThreshold: 0` keeps this proactive movement disabled.
+
+Local Codex CLI requests in automatic Pool mode also consider stored Main Account when the client
+sends its own ChatGPT token. Direct mode, explicit account selectors, Reserve, and remote requests
+retain caller credential isolation. If stored authentication is unavailable, the validated caller
+token can still serve as a request-only fallback.
+
 Rotation does not protect against provider enforcement; multi-account use may violate provider terms.
 
